  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1110 AM CDT Sun May 10 2026\n\nThrough the coming week, there will be a couple of low-end \nchances for rain, but nothing much. This is bad news for drought \nconditions which are likely to worsen. The bright side is an \nextremely low potential for any hazardous weather.\n\nOtherwise, temperatures will bounce around a little through the\nweek, generally in the pleasant/normal 70s and lower 80s. But, \nthe pleasantries may slip away as extended models show the broad \ntrough over the eastern states moving out as strong ridging moves \nour way. This may set us up for our first 90+ degree days of 2026 \nby the weekend. Along with the warmth, we could see the start of a\ndiurnal shower/storm pattern with 10-30 percent coverage each \nafternoon.",
